f 17592186045417] [17592186078557 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078557 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234063 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078557 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234064 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078557 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234065 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078557 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186237815 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078557 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186244013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078557 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078557 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186297275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078557 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311952 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078557 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311953 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078557 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311954 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078557 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078557 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186329758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078557 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186329761 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078557 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186329795 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078557 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186362630 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078557 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186364206 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078557 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186364289 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078557 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating the Limit of a Rational Function with a Radical in the Denominator" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078557 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186078359 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078557 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "045722b6-b558-522b-86e1-322c64e2848f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078635 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186079469 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078635 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186079470 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078635 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186079500 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078635 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078635 #edb/ref 1045 "Calculating Limits of Radical Functions Using Conjugate Multiplication" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078635 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186079469 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078635 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050225 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078635 #edb/ref 1050 720.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186078635 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "da39b17e-570c-50b3-ac5f-dba85525f10f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079469 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186079470 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079469 #edb/ref 1061 453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079469 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d20c032d-424d-59b2-947c-bd6f83dc0b44" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079469 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186079646 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079470 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186079500 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079470 #edb/ref 1061 454 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079470 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e7f2241e-1a39-5fd2-bf4c-e20365acd894" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079470 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186078536 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079500 #edb/ref 1061 458 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079500 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "93db8b23-0bbc-5091-a87e-379d4484afba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079500 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186078557 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079646 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose that we want to calculate the following limit:\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x \\to 1} \\frac{\\sqrt{x} - 1}{x - 1}\n$$\n\nIf we try to evaluate the limit by directly substituting $x=1,$ we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-1}{x-1} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{1}-1}{1-1}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, if we simplify the fraction before evaluating the limit, we obtain a more clear result. To simplify the fraction, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator of the function by the **conjugate** of the numerator.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of $\\sqrt{x}-1,$ we simply switch the sign between the two terms to get $\\sqrt{x}+ 1.$ \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\require{cancel}\n\\lim_{x\\to 1} \\frac{\\sqrt{x} - 1} {x - 1}\n\t&= \\lim_{x\\to 1} \\frac{\\sqrt{x} - 1} {x - 1} \\cdot\\dfrac{\\sqrt{x} + 1}{\\sqrt{x} + 1}\t\\\n\t&=\\lim_{x\\to 1} \\dfrac{(\\sqrt{x} - 1)(\\sqrt{x} +1)} {(x-1)(\\sqrt{x} + 1)}\\\n        &=\\lim_{x\\to 1} \\dfrac{\\left(\\sqrt{x}\\right)^2 - 1^2} {(x-1)(\\sqrt{x} + 1)}\\\n\t&=\\lim_{x\\to 1} \\dfrac{x-1} {(x-1)(\\sqrt{x} + 1)}\\\n\t&=\\lim_{x\\to 1} \\dfrac{\\cancel{x-1}} {\\cancel{(x-1)}(\\sqrt{x} + 1)}\\\n\t&=\\lim_{x\\to 1} \\dfrac1{\\sqrt{x} + 1}\\\n        &=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{1} +1}\\\n\t&=\\dfrac{1}{2}\n}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079646 #edb/ref 1065 250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079646 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "73481739-fdce-5a28-84e1-5145ea62af87" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079646 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087880 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049362 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087880 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186088191 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087880 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186088192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087880 #edb/ref 1039 "Constructing an Expression that Represents the Derivative of a Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087880 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186087431 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087880 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "5e905212-8796-5742-a83e-892fdf66eced" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087881 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186088189 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087881 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186088190 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087881 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233549 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087881 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186235416 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087881 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating the Derivative of a Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087881 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186087432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087881 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "9c6f3c71-d11b-59af-bad6-5f5c0ff6634f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087898 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186088823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087898 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186088824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087898 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186088827 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087898 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186088828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087898 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087898 #edb/ref 1045 "Defining the Derivative Using Derivative Notation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087898 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186088823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087898 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048904 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087898 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "bb9db01e-936b-52c3-b219-e1950b5ae188" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088823 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186088824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088823 #edb/ref 1061 605 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088823 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "454777cc-cdc5-5db8-b536-5b674f1199d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088823 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186088899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088824 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186088827 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088824 #edb/ref 1061 606 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088824 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "37cc5660-640c-5836-92be-6ff27138fdcb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088824 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186087880 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088827 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186088828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088827 #edb/ref 1061 609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088827 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1b806b59-9344-54a4-8988-8cb76d4286c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088827 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186088900 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088828 #edb/ref 1061 613 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088828 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2c77b3ab-7255-54eb-92d4-2ad06b30a0cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088828 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186087881 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088899 #edb/ref 1064 "The instantaneous rate of change of a function $f(x)$ at the point $x=a$, denoted $f'(a)$, is given by the limit\n\n$$\nf'(a) = \\lim_{h\\to 0}\\dfrac{f(a+h) - f(a)}{h}\n$$\n\nThis formula works for a specific point $x=a$. If we want a method that works for a *general* point $x$, then we substitute $a=x$ in the formula and get\n\n$$\nf'(x) = \\lim_{h\\to 0}\\dfrac{f(x+h) - f(x)}{h}\n$$\n\nThe function $f'(x)$ is called the **derivative of $f(x)$ with respect to $x$**. It gives the slope of the tangent line to the curve $y=f(x)$ at a general point with coordinates $(x,f(x))$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088899 #edb/ref 1065 327 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088899 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "098fd6b0-306b-544a-9e7f-b301ff48f525" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088899 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088900 #edb/ref 1064 "For a given curve $y=f(x)$, the derivative can be represented using several different notations. They are\n\n$$\nf'(x),\\qquad y'(x), \\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}f}{\\textrm{d}x}, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\n$$\n\nIn words, the term $y'(x)$ is said like\n\n- \"$y$ prime of $x$,\" or\n- \"$y$ prime,\" or sometimes\n- \"$y$ dash.\"\n\nThe term\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\n$$\n\nis said like \"dee $y$ by dee $x$.\"\n\nThe important thing to remember is that they all represent the same thing, the derivative." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088900 #edb/ref 1065 329 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088900 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "cda9f5ac-1ad1-50ce-8bc4-ee5f3be5fd92" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088900 #edb/ref 1067 "Alternative Definitions For the Derivative" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096628 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096628 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048922 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096628 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049317 #edb/ref 